  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A photograph of a midtown Manhattan street under construction, with a long grey cartoon fence running down the sidewalk, a green copper skybridge between towers, a red building with a scribbled sign, and a few pedestrians redrawn as outlined figures, labelled SP 47 2024.",
    "description": "A portrait format digital piece on a photograph inside a white border, captioned SP 47 2024 at lower left and MATT CRUMP at lower right. A canyon of midtown buildings: a red painted wall and a gold stone building at left, an ornate green copper skybridge crossing between two towers at upper centre, glass towers at the far end, and a dark glass building with a colourful reflective facade at right. A vertical red sign on the left building has its lettering replaced with white scribbles. The sidewalk at lower left is lined by a long construction fence redrawn as a flat grey cartoon wall with black outlines, receding to the vanishing point. A few pedestrians near the fence are redrawn as outlined figures with blank faces: a figure in a maroon top with a red bag at centre, figures in purple and white in the distance. A small red hydrant creature stands at right. The sky is pale blue.",
    "impression": "Minimal cartooning, as the process note says: the drawing picks one thing, the construction fence, and turns it into a long grey ribbon, and otherwise leaves the canyon alone. The copper skybridge is the real star. It reads as a study in restraint, the photograph allowed to be the picture with a single cartoon intervention.",
